The final costing, including advert design and production, comes to 45,600 RMB.

245
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:09,870
We want payment 10 working days before publication, or we will cancel the ad.

246
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Thanks for...

247
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Whoa.

248
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,360
Okay, back up a second, Tracy.

249
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,070
That's too direct.

250
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:22,690
Can I suggest you say, please note that the final payment is due two working weeks before publication.

251
00:14:23,450 --> 00:14:24,810
You don't want to offend her.

252
00:14:25,110 --> 00:14:25,450
Oops.

253
00:14:25,770 --> 00:14:26,750
Okay, you're right.

254
00:14:27,150 --> 00:14:30,010
Then I can just end with, all the best, Tracy.

255
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:36,240
Maybe I'd play it safe and just finish with, yours sincerely.

256
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:36,850
That's more professional.

257
00:14:37,590 --> 00:14:39,490
Oh, Melanie, you're a lifesaver.

258
00:14:39,970 --> 00:14:40,270
Thank you.

259
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:55,820
So talking about ending formal emails or emails that you're writing to clients, colleagues, we can say sincerely, and your name, sincerely, Marco.

260
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,820
You can say, all the best, best regards.

261
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:12,200
Now I've noticed that some people who aren't native English speakers, sometimes they will close a letter, maybe even a formal letter, saying, yours truly, Marco, for example.

262
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:15,460
Is that really appropriate for a business setting or a client?

263
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:17,160
I would not use yours truly.

264
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:26,280
Maybe if you're trying to build a relationship with your client and you're very honest, but it seems to me to be very personal.

265
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,380
Very romantic.

266
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:28,340
Yes, yours truly.

267
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:38,960
So I would say in that case, use sincerely or kind regards, or regards, which are a little bit more professional and less emotional.

268
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:46,720
If you want to have a romantic letter, you can say, all my love or love or yours truly or yours faithfully.

269
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:57,020
This is a very important topic, I think, because many times in school we do learn how to write letters, but usually they are more personal letters.

270
00:15:57,360 --> 00:16:04,620
And so we memorize that usually at the end of the email or the end of the letter, you say yours, Marco, or yours truly, Marco.

271
00:16:05,260 --> 00:16:09,320
And although it is correct, it's not really appropriate for a professional setting.

272
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:10,160
That's right.

273
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:20,760
Just a reminder, if you're signing off your email or your letter and you're at an office, you're in your company, you want to say best or best regards or some of the things that we talked about here today.

274
00:16:21,020 --> 00:16:21,400
Very good.

275
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:21,880
All right.

276
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:27,120
So if you have any questions or any other doubts, you can always find us at EnglishPod.com and we'll see you guys there.

277
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:27,500
Bye.

278
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:35,579
Bye-bye.
